  "root_page": {
    "title": "Atomic Habits OS",
    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "callout",
        "text": "Welcome to Atomic Habits OS. You do not rise to the level of your goals; you fall to the level of your systems. Use this workspace to transform habits into permanent identity traits."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading_1",
        "text": "Daily Command Center"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Complete your daily habits by ticking the checkmark in Today's Checklist view below. Focus on daily non-negotiables first before taking on flexible items."
      },
      {
        "type": "to_do",
        "text": "Complete Morning Hydration & Mindfulness"
      },
      {
        "type": "to_do",
        "text": "Protect primary Deep Work Sprint block"
      },
      {
        "type": "to_do",
        "text": "Execute evening digital shutdown & review checklist"
      },
      {
        "type": "divider",
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "type": "heading_2",
        "text": "Identity Pillars & Core Systems"
      },
      {
        "type": "quote",
        "text": "True behavior change is identity change. The goal is not to read a book; the goal is to become a reader."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Link each routine to an underlying Life Area. Reinforce identity evidence every time you complete a check-in."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading_2",
        "text": "Weekly Review Rhythm"
      },
      {
        "type": "bulleted_list",
        "text": "Reflect every Sunday on habit friction and adherence scores."
      },
      {
        "type": "bulleted_list",
        "text": "Optimize your environment rather than relying on sheer willpower."
      },
      {
        "type": "bulleted_list",
        "text": "Never miss twice: if you fail one day, prioritize showing up the next day even for 2 minutes."
      }
    ],
    "sub_pages": [
      {
        "title": "How to Use This Template",
        "sections": [
          {
            "type": "heading_1",
            "text": "Quick Start Guide"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "This OS follows James Clear's Four Laws of Behavior Change: Make it Obvious, Make it Attractive, Make it Easy, and Make it Satisfying."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading_2",
            "text": "Step-by-Step Workflow"
          },
          {
            "type": "numbered_list",
            "text": "Define your Life Areas: Articulate your identity statements in the Life Areas database."
          },
          {
            "type": "numbered_list",
            "text": "Configure Habits: Add target routines, assign them to a life pillar, and set preferred times of day."
          },
          {
            "type": "numbered_list",
            "text": "Daily Check-Ins: Each morning or evening, open the Daily Logs view to log completion and rate your energy level."
          },
          {
            "type": "numbered_list",
            "text": "Weekly Reviews: At the close of each week, run a review to spot recurring friction and adjust your environment."
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "text": "Pro-tip: Keep your active habits under 5 when starting out. Master consistency before scaling complexity."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Habit Stacking & Implementation Playbook",
        "sections": [
          {
            "type": "heading_1",
            "text": "The Habit Stacking Framework"
          },
          {
            "type": "quote",
            "text": "After [CURRENT HABIT], I will [NEW HABIT]."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading_2",
            "text": "Proven Habit Stacks"
          },
          {
            "type": "bulleted_list",
            "text": "Morning Vitality: After my feet hit the floor, I will drink 1L of water with sea salt."
          },
          {
            "type": "bulleted_list",
            "text": "Mindful Transition: After I close my laptop for the day, I will write down 3 wins and meditate for 10 minutes."
          },
          {
            "type": "bulleted_list",
            "text": "Deep Sleep Cue: After I brush my teeth at night, I will place my smartphone across the room and pick up my book."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading_2",
            "text": "Temptation Bundling"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Pair an action you need to do with an action you want to do. Only listen to your favorite podcast while doing cardio or meal prepping."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Monthly Analytics & Data Archiving",
        "sections": [
          {
            "type": "heading_1",
            "text": "Managing Long-Term Consistency"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Over time, your Daily Logs database will accumulate hundreds of entries. Keep Notion running smoothly with these archiving tips."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading_2",
            "text": "End-of-Month Protocol"
          },
          {
            "type": "bulleted_list",
            "text": "Check Total Check-ins rollup on each habit to inspect completion volume."
          },
          {
            "type": "bulleted_list",
            "text": "Archive past logs older than 90 days into an Archive database or lock older rows behind date filters."
          },
          {
            "type": "bulleted_list",
            "text": "Deactivate obsolete habits by unchecking the Active property to remove them from your active views."
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "text": "Remember: The scorecard is feedback, not self-worth. Iterate on the friction points until consistency becomes frictionless."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}